# Pinned models for the numerical-correctness gate, targeting
# jina-embeddings-v5-text-nano-retrieval (EuroBERT-210m, last-token pooling, dim 768).
#
# TWO artifacts:
#   1. CORRECTNESS_MODEL_URL/SHA256 — the GGUF the static llama.cpp archives load, for the
#      §2 tuned-vs-generic and §4 self-consistency checks AND the §1 golden-parity side.
#      This is the DEPLOYED quant: IQ4_NL (has the ARM interleaved-GEMM dotprod path on
#      Graviton2 — see notes on IQ4_XS having no GEMM path).
#   2. CORRECTNESS_GOLDEN_MODEL_ID/REV — the FP32 PyTorch model (safetensors) that
#      scripts/gen-golden.py runs offline via sentence-transformers to produce golden.tsv,
#      the independent §1 reference. Pin REV so the golden is reproducible.
#
# The `:-` defaults let CI override via repo variables (vars.CORRECTNESS_MODEL_URL /
# vars.CORRECTNESS_MODEL_SHA256) without editing this file. correctness.sh fails closed if
# the GGUF sha is empty from both.
#
# REQUIRED before the gate goes live: fill CORRECTNESS_MODEL_SHA256 for the exact GGUF
# below (curl the URL, `sha256sum`), and run scripts/gen-golden.py to produce golden.tsv
# against the SAME IQ4_NL GGUF vs FP32.
CORRECTNESS_MODEL_URL="${CORRECTNESS_MODEL_URL:-https://huggingface.co/jinaai/jina-embeddings-v5-text-nano-retrieval-GGUF/resolve/main/v5-nano-retrieval-IQ4_NL.gguf}"
CORRECTNESS_MODEL_SHA256="${CORRECTNESS_MODEL_SHA256:-}"

# FP32 golden source (PyTorch/safetensors) — used ONLY by scripts/gen-golden.py, offline.
CORRECTNESS_GOLDEN_MODEL_ID="${CORRECTNESS_GOLDEN_MODEL_ID:-jinaai/jina-embeddings-v5-text-nano-retrieval}"
# Pin the HF revision the golden was generated from (main sha at authoring time). Bump +
# regenerate golden.tsv deliberately.
CORRECTNESS_GOLDEN_MODEL_REV="${CORRECTNESS_GOLDEN_MODEL_REV:-main}"
